.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Command history management using GNU Readline\&. 

This module provides functions to initialize the command history subsystem, determine the history file path, load history from a file, and save history to a file\&.

.PP
The history file is determined by checking the $HISTFILE environment variable first, and if that is not set, falling back to $HOME/\&.sh_history\&. The history is loaded into memory at shell startup and saved back to disk on shell exit\&.

.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
pulgamecanica 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "char * history_file_path (void )"

.PP
Determine the path to the history file based on environment variables\&. Follows POSIX-compliant lookup order: first checks $HISTFILE, then falls back to $HOME/\&.sh_history\&. Returns a malloc'd string that the caller must free\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A malloc'd string with the history file path, or NULL if neither variable is set or valid\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void history_init (\fBt_shell\fP * shell)"

.PP
Initialize the history subsystem\&. This sets up readline's history handling and loads the history file if available\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIshell\fP The main shell state struct, used to store the history file path\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void history_load (const char * file_path)"

.PP
Load the command history from a file into readline's in-memory history list\&. This function uses readline's \fRread_history()\fP to populate the history list\&. If \fRfile_path\fP is NULL, this function does nothing\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIfile_path\fP The path to the history file to load, or NULL to skip loading\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void history_save (const char * file_path)"

.PP
Save the in-memory command history list to a file\&. This function uses readline's \fRwrite_history()\fP to write the history list to disk\&. If \fRfile_path\fP is NULL, this function does nothing\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIfile_path\fP The path to the history file to save, or NULL to skip saving\&. 
.RE
.PP

